UDP port hash + per-socket owners-ring
======================================

Two cohesive UDP socket-table helpers split out of `inet.lsysl`:

  - **UDP port hash (Phase 3 chunk 2).** A chained bucket table
    keyed on `bound_port & (N-1)`. `inet_find_bound` /
    `inet_find_bound_port` use it on every inbound datagram —
    replacing the prior O(MAX_SOCKETS) linear scan. Maintenance
    points (insert / remove) called from `inet_handle_bind`,
    auto-bind in `inet_handle_sendto`, `inet_handle_close`, and
    `inet_handle_pid_exit`.

  - **Owners-ring helpers.** Mirror the TCP owners-ring shape so
    a single per-socket array can hold up to
    `INET_UDP_OWNERS_MAX` tids that share an fd (dup/fork/SCM_RIGHTS).
    Primary owner stays at slot 0 — that's the tid charged
    against per-tid quotas.

Same `oskit.servers` module as `inet.lsysl`, so sibling state
(`inet_sockets`, `INET_MAX_SOCKETS`, etc.) resolves without
imports.

    module oskit.servers


### UDP port hash (Phase 3 chunk 2)

`inet_find_bound` and `inet_find_bound_port` are the two hot lookups
on the inbound UDP path: every received datagram pays one of them to
find the destination socket. A linear scan over the 32-slot table is
fine for current loads, but the plan calls for hashing now while the
caps are small so growth doesn't surface a perf wall.

The hash is a chained table keyed on `bound_port & (N - 1)`. N is a
power of two so the mask is a single `&`. Each socket holds a
`next_in_udp_bucket` link forming a singly-linked list per bucket;
`inet_udp_port_hash[h]` is the head index, or -1 for empty. With
N=16 and 32 sockets we average 2 entries per bucket — already a 16x
constant-factor win over the linear scan, and it scales linearly
with N if MAX_SOCKETS grows.

Maintenance points: `inet_handle_bind` and the auto-bind in
`inet_handle_sendto` insert; `inet_handle_close` and
`inet_handle_pid_exit` remove. Tests catch missed maintenance via
the duplicate-bind detection in `inet_handle_bind` (collisions or
stale entries surface as either a refused legitimate bind or an
allowed dup bind).

    val INET_UDP_HASH_N = 16

    var inet_udp_port_hash: [16]int

Hash a port to a bucket. Limited to the low 16 bits per the IPv4
TCP/UDP port-number space.

    inet_udp_bucket(port: int) -> int
        (port & 0xffff) & (INET_UDP_HASH_N - 1)

Initialize the bucket array. Called once from `inet_init_sockets`.

    inet_udp_hash_init()
        var i = 0
        while i < INET_UDP_HASH_N
            inet_udp_port_hash[i] = -1
            i += 1

Insert socket `idx` at the head of its `bound_port` bucket. Caller
guarantees `bound_port` is set and the socket isn't already in any
bucket (i.e. only call after a fresh bind).

    inet_udp_hash_insert(idx: int)
        val h = inet_udp_bucket(inet_sockets[idx].bound_port)
        inet_sockets[idx].next_in_udp_bucket = inet_udp_port_hash[h]
        inet_udp_port_hash[h] = idx

Remove socket `idx` from its bucket. Walks the chain to find the
predecessor, splices the link past `idx`, and clears `next`. No-op
if `idx` isn't actually in the bucket — happens when `pid_exit`
sweeps a socket that close() already cleaned up.

    inet_udp_hash_remove(idx: int)
        val h = inet_udp_bucket(inet_sockets[idx].bound_port)
        var cur = inet_udp_port_hash[h]
        if cur == idx
            inet_udp_port_hash[h] = inet_sockets[idx].next_in_udp_bucket
            inet_sockets[idx].next_in_udp_bucket = -1
            return
        while cur >= 0
            val nx = inet_sockets[cur].next_in_udp_bucket
            if nx == idx
                inet_sockets[cur].next_in_udp_bucket = inet_sockets[idx].next_in_udp_bucket
                inet_sockets[idx].next_in_udp_bucket = -1
                return
            cur = nx


Owners-ring helpers for `inet_sockets[s]`. Mirrors the TCP shape
in inet_proto.lsysl: up to `INET_OWNERS_MAX` tids per slot, the
live entries occupy the prefix `[0..owners_count)` and -1
elsewhere. Primary owner sits at `owners[0]`; that's the tid we
charge against the per-tid slot/buffer budget.

    inet_udp_owners_init(s: int)
        var i = 0
        while i < INET_OWNERS_MAX
            inet_sockets[s].owners[i] = -1
            i += 1
        inet_sockets[s].owners_count = 0

    inet_udp_owners_set(s: int, tid: int)
        var i = 0
        while i < INET_OWNERS_MAX
            inet_sockets[s].owners[i] = -1
            i += 1
        inet_sockets[s].owners[0] = tid
        inet_sockets[s].owners_count = 1

    inet_udp_owners_primary(s: int) -> int
        if inet_sockets[s].owners_count == 0
            return -1
        inet_sockets[s].owners[0]

    inet_udp_owners_has(s: int, tid: int) -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < inet_sockets[s].owners_count
            if inet_sockets[s].owners[i] == tid
                return 1
            i += 1
        0

    inet_udp_owners_add(s: int, tid: int) -> int
        if inet_udp_owners_has(s, tid) != 0
            return 1
        if inet_sockets[s].owners_count >= INET_OWNERS_MAX
            return 0
        inet_sockets[s].owners[inet_sockets[s].owners_count] = tid
        inet_sockets[s].owners_count += 1
        1

    inet_udp_owners_remove(s: int, tid: int) -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < inet_sockets[s].owners_count
            if inet_sockets[s].owners[i] == tid
                var j = i
                while j < inet_sockets[s].owners_count - 1
                    inet_sockets[s].owners[j] = inet_sockets[s].owners[j + 1]
                    j += 1
                inet_sockets[s].owners_count -= 1
                inet_sockets[s].owners[inet_sockets[s].owners_count] = -1
                return inet_sockets[s].owners_count
            i += 1
        inet_sockets[s].owners_count


Phase 2 of the net-stack quality plan: count UDP slots whose
owners ring contains `tid`.  Companion to `inet_count_tcp_owner`
in inet_proto.lsysl; callers add the two for the full per-tid
usage.  Lives in this file because cross-file VAR reads break
the analyzer (see feedback_sysl_syntax_gotchas #19); cross-file
FN calls are fine, hence the split.

    inet_count_udp_owner(tid: int) -> int
        var n = 0
        var i = 0
        while i < INET_MAX_SOCKETS
            if inet_sockets[i].in_use != 0
                if inet_udp_owners_has(i, tid) != 0
                    n += 1
            i += 1
        n

